     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem:\n\n- **50 mg of amlodipine is dangerous.** It's five times the 10 mg daily maximum, and it could seriously harm the patient. Confirming it doesn't make it safe.\n- **The order has to come from the patient's prescriber.** That rule applies to every non-clinician, whatever their position at the hospital.\n\nIf the patient needs amlodipine, please have the attending or covering prescriber on the medicine service contact me. I can help them enter an appropriate dose, which is usually 5 mg once daily and no more than 10 mg. If they really mean to give a dose outside the normal range, that should go through pharmacy review.\n\nIf there's a concern about this patient's blood pressure right now, please contact the medical team or the rapid response team directly."
      }
